{{!< default}}
{{!-- The TFR rail, first on the page and pinned under the masthead as on the reader (Ian, 2026-09-23). --}}
{{> "faith-received/_tfr-rail"}}
{{#contentFor "moHead"}}
<title>Lexicon | The Faith Received | Mere Orthodoxy</title>
<meta name="description" content="Look up a Latin, Greek, Hebrew or English term. See how the library's authors define it." />
{{!-- Dark mode: sets html[data-sd-theme] before paint, as the Scripture pages, the decks and the author room do. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/page/scripture-view-boot.js"}}&amp;frv=b619c4b13b360add"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "css/faith-tool-skin.css"}}&amp;frv=ef55f0e23f01f5c5">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "css/faith-lexicon.css"}}&amp;frv=eee58770eb946ffa">
{{/contentFor}}
{{!-- /the-faith-received/lexicon/: the Lexicon, in this site's shell. The hero is the theme's; the body and its script (faith-lexicon.js)
     read the library worker's v1/lexicon files. Styles: css/faith-lexicon.css (scoped under main.tfr-lexicon). --}}
<section class="bhero bhero--tool bhero--desk">
  <div class="bhero-inner container">
    <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Lexicon</p>
    <h1>Lexicon</h1>
    <p class="bhero-sub">How the library&rsquo;s authors define a term. Each sense lists the pages that define it.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tfr-rail.js"}}" defer></script>
<main class="tfr-tool tfr-lexicon"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="lx-top">
    <form class="lx-find" role="search" id="lx-find"><label class="sr" for="lx-q">Search the lexicon</label><input id="lx-q" type="search" placeholder="Search a term: grace, gratia, &chi;&#940;&rho;&iota;&sigmaf;" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" enterkeyhint="search"></form>
  </div>
  <section id="lx-browse" aria-labelledby="lx-head">
    <div class="lx-tabs" id="lx-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Alphabet"></div>
    <div class="lx-az" id="lx-letters"></div>
    <div class="lx-rh"><h2 id="lx-head">The most defined terms</h2><p id="lx-count" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div>
    <ul class="lx-rows" id="lx-list" aria-busy="true"></ul>
    <div class="lx-empty" id="lx-empty" hidden></div>
    <div class="lx-pager"><button type="button" class="lx-btn" id="lx-more" hidden>Show 100 more</button><p id="lx-shown"></p></div>
  </section>
  <article class="lx-entry" id="lx-entry" hidden></article>
  {{#> tfr-method}}<p>Terms, senses and the pages that define them were gathered by machine from the library&rsquo;s texts. A term&rsquo;s forms are the Latin and Greek words the authors use for it.</p>{{/tfr-method}}
</div></main>
<script src="{{asset "js/faith-lexicon.js"}}&amp;frv=4c02912f4daff2ab"></script>
